= Coalition Formation Impossible in Prussia - New Elections

**No viable coalition could be formed in the Prussian Landtag.**

All major parties have attempted and failed to build a majority. The Landtag is deadlocked.

[? if no_majority_elections_prussia = 1 : This is the first time the Prussian Landtag has failed to elect a Minister-President. ?]

Under Article 45 of the Prussian Constitution, the deadlocked Landtag will be dissolved and new elections held in **[+ next_election_month_prussia : month +] [+ next_election_year_prussia +]**.

A caretaker Staatsministerium (Geschäftsführendes Ministerium) will administer the state until then, but cannot pass major legislation.

**Political Impact:**
- Public frustration with parliamentary democracy in Prussia grows
- Extremist parties will use this deadlock in their campaign against the "Weimar system"
- Coalition negotiations will resume after the election

[? if no_majority_elections_prussia = 1 : If the next Landtag election also produces no viable coalition, the outgoing cabinet may be forced to continue on a caretaker basis indefinitely, or the Reich government may seek grounds to intervene. ?]

- @accept_elections_prussia: Accept the electoral solution

@accept_elections_prussia
on-arrival: coalition_dissent_prussia += 2; left_dissent += 3

New Landtag elections have been scheduled. The campaign will be dominated by questions about governmental stability in Prussia.

Our party must prepare for what may be a crucial electoral test in the largest German state.










@presidential_crisis_prussia
on-arrival: {!
// ============================================================
// NO COALITION POSSIBLE - PRUSSIAN CONSTITUTIONAL CRISIS
// Prussia has no President with Article 48 powers of its own;
// deadlock instead produces a caretaker Staatsministerium under
// Art. 59 of the Prussian Constitution, or — if conditions allow
// — sets the stage for Reich-level intervention (the historical
// "Preußenschlag" template).
// ============================================================

Q.caretaker_government_prussia = 1;
Q.in_minority_government_prussia = 1;
Q.spd_in_government_prussia = Q.spd_in_government_prussia; // caretaker retains last cabinet's party flags by default
Q.staatsministerium_geschaeftsfuehrend = 1;

Q.interior_minister_party_prussia = Q.interior_minister_party_prussia || 'I';
Q.justice_minister_party_prussia = Q.justice_minister_party_prussia || 'I';
Q.finance_minister_party_prussia = Q.finance_minister_party_prussia || 'I';
Q.trade_minister_party_prussia = Q.trade_minister_party_prussia || 'I';
Q.agriculture_minister_party_prussia = Q.agriculture_minister_party_prussia || 'I';
Q.publicworks_minister_party_prussia = Q.publicworks_minister_party_prussia || 'I';
Q.kultus_minister_party_prussia = Q.kultus_minister_party_prussia || 'I';

// The incumbent Minister-President (if any) continues in a
// caretaker capacity per Art. 59 Abs. 2, unless a Preußenschlag
// scenario is active.
if (Q.preussenschlag_active) {
    Q.ministerpresident = "Reichskommissar (vakant)";
    Q.mp_party_prussia = "I";
    Q.presidential_powers_active = 1;
    Q.pro_republic -= 12;
    Q.coup_progress += 3;
} else {
    Q.ministerpresident = Q.ministerpresident || "Braun";
    Q.mp_party_prussia = Q.mp_party_prussia || "SPD";
}

Q.pro_republic -= 4;
Q.workers_spd -= 2;
Q.new_middle_spd -= 1;
Q.old_middle_spd -= 1;
Q.coup_progress += 1;
!}

= Constitutional Crisis in Prussia

**After [+ no_majority_elections_prussia +] consecutive failed attempts to elect a Minister-President, the Prussian Landtag has reached an impasse.**

All major parties have repeatedly failed to build a majority government. Under Article 59 of the Prussian Constitution, the outgoing Staatsministerium continues in a **caretaker capacity** ("geschäftsführend"), unable to resign or be replaced until a successor commands a majority.

[? if not preussenschlag_active : **Minister-President (caretaker):** [+ ministerpresident +] [? if mp_party_prussia != 'I' : ([+ mp_party_prussia +]) ?] continues to administer the state government pending a resolution. ?]

[? if preussenschlag_active : The Reich government has seized on the deadlock to argue that Prussia can no longer maintain order, and has moved to install a Reich Commissioner in place of the elected Staatsministerium. This is an unprecedented and constitutionally dubious intervention into a state's internal affairs. ?]

This caretaker arrangement is inherently unstable. New Landtag elections, further negotiation, or Reich-level intervention may all follow.

[? if no_majority_elections_prussia >= 3 : After three consecutive electoral failures to produce a Prussian government, many Germans — on both left and right — question whether Prussia's parliamentary system can still function. ?]

- @accept_crisis_prussia: Accept the caretaker arrangement

@accept_crisis_prussia
on-arrival: coalition_dissent_prussia += 3 if spd_in_government_prussia = 0; left_dissent += 6 if spd_toleration_prussia = 1; political_crisis_level += 1

The Prussian government crisis continues under a caretaker administration. [? if preussenschlag_active : Many in our party see this as the death of Prussian self-government and a dangerous precedent for the whole Reich. ?]

Parliamentary democracy in Prussia has suffered a serious blow.

# ============================================
# SPECIAL COALITION SCENARIOS (PRUSSIA)
# ============================================

@popular_front_special_prussia
title: Attempt to form a Prussian Popular Front
subtitle: SPD + KPD + Z + [+ ddp_name +] ([+ spd_r_prussia + kpd_r_prussia + z_r_prussia + ddp_r_prussia +]%)
view-if: coalition_type_prussia = 'popular_front' and popular_front_possible_prussia = 1
on-arrival: coup_progress += 1; in_popular_front_prussia = 1; kpd_relation += 8; z_relation += 8; pro_republic += 4
achievement: preussen_volksfront

Through extraordinary negotiations, a Popular Front has been formed in the Prussian Landtag!

The Conciliator leadership of the KPD and the progressive leadership of Joseph Joos in the Centre Party have made this historic coalition possible in Germany's largest state.

This is an unprecedented moment: Communists, Socialists, and Catholics united in defense of Prussian democracy against the Nazi threat.

However, the right-wing views this as a betrayal. Agitation against "Red Prussia" will intensify.

@left_front_special_prussia
title: Attempt to form a Prussian Left Front
subtitle: SPD + KPD [? if sapd_formed : + SAPD ?] ([+ spd_r_prussia + kpd_r_prussia + sapd_r_prussia +]%)
view-if: coalition_type_prussia = 'left_front' and left_front_possible_prussia = 1
on-arrival: coup_progress += 2; capital_strike_progress += 1; in_left_front_prussia = 1; kpd_relation += 12; reichswehr_loyalty -= 0.05
achievement: preussen_einheitsfront

The Left Front has been formed in Prussia! Workers' unity has finally been achieved in the largest German state.

For the first time, Social Democrats and Communists will govern together in Prussia. This is either the dawn of a new socialist Prussia or a disaster waiting to happen.

The bourgeois parties are horrified. The right-wing press screams of "Bolshevism on the Spree." The Reich government watches closely for any pretext to intervene.

[? if sapd_formed : The SAPD's participation bridges the gap between the two larger parties. ?]

@nazi_coalition_warning_prussia
title: The Nazis demand power in Prussia
view-if: nsdap_r_prussia >= 30 and coalition_type_prussia = 'far_right'
on-arrival: coup_progress += 3; pro_republic -= 12; sa_strength += 100

**WARNING: NAZI COALITION FORMED IN PRUSSIA**

[+ nsdap_leader +] has entered the Prussian state government. The Nazis now control the police apparatus of Germany's largest state — a catastrophic development for the republic.

# ============================================================
# KPD COALITION GOALS (PRUSSIA, if in government)
# ============================================================

@kpd_coalition_demands_prussia
title: The KPD presents its coalition demands in Prussia
view-if: kpd_in_government_prussia and not kpd_goals_seen_prussia
on-arrival: kpd_goals_seen_prussia = 1; kpd_coalition_dissent_prussia = 0

The Communists have agreed to join the Prussian state government, but they have demands:

**KPD Coalition Goals (Prussia):**

1. **Interior Ministry:** Must rein in the Prussian political police's actions against the left and crack down on fascist organizations
2. **Kultus Ministry:** Must expand welfare provision for the unemployed
3. **Trade Ministry:** Must implement socialist economic planning in state enterprises
4. **Finance Ministry:** Must tax the wealthy heavily

The KPD will track our progress on these goals. If we fail to meet their expectations, they may withdraw from the coalition.

[? if in_popular_front_prussia : Notably, the KPD has moderated some demands due to the Popular Front arrangement with the Centre Party. ?]

[? if in_left_front_prussia : The KPD is being more aggressive in the Left Front, demanding radical changes immediately. ?]

- @accept_kpd_goals_prussia: We will work with the KPD on these goals
- @reject_kpd_goals_prussia: These demands are too extreme

@accept_kpd_goals_prussia
on-arrival: kpd_coalition_dissent_prussia -= 4; left_dissent -= 4; labor_dissent -= 4; reformist_dissent += 8; neorevisionist_dissent += 8

We have agreed to work toward the KPD's policy goals in Prussia. The left wing of our party is pleased, but moderates are concerned.

@reject_kpd_goals_prussia
on-arrival: kpd_coalition_dissent_prussia += 8; kpd_relation -= 8; left_dissent += 4

We have rejected the KPD's most radical demands in Prussia. They are unhappy, but remain in the coalition for now.

